  - data quality
  - readability
abstract: >-
  Applies a declare-then-test provenance check to the 24 public corpora of the
  UniversalCEFR collection (13 languages, 65,037 rows). The schema is uniform,
  and an exhaustive inversion of every text finds no corpus sharing text with
  another except one pair: two entries declaring different repositories, papers
  and licences, where 130 texts are identical and 324 of 325 match one to one
  with 100% label agreement. Two corpora repeat their own texts structurally
  under conflicting CEFR levels, the label field holds 17 distinct strings, and
  the row-level licence disagrees with the dataset card in 13 of 24 corpora.
  Every published figure is printed by the script; redistributes no data.
